sections.Testkonzept/Testaufbau:
The FAM consists of 18 items with a seven-point response format ("1 = trifft nicht zu" to "7 = trifft zu"), which comprise the following four scales (Rheinberg et al., 2001, S. 58, S. 59):
(1) Fear of failure (items 5, 9, 12, 16, 18);
(2) Challenge (items 6, 8, 10, 15);
(3) Probability of success (items 2, 3, 13, 14; items 3 and 14 are reversed);
(4) Interest (items 1, 4, 7, 11).
The scale fear of failure describes the negative incentive of failure. It is assumed that a person cannot work optimally because of the pressure. The scale probability of success indicates how confident someone is of mastering a task. This can lie in the person (own ability) or in the task (too easy). The scale interest refers to the appreciation of the task content. The scale challenge assesses the task with regard to its achievement-related relevance. With the exception of the scale interest, the scales have an achievement-related character (Rheinberg et al., 2001, S. 59).
